Prompt 1
You are dispatched to a 25 year old female- Altered mental status.

On your way to the call name 3 things that you learned about in this course that can cause altered mental status (a differential diagnosis for altered mental status).  You must have at least one medical cause and one traumatic cause.

An example (that will not be given points if provided as your answer) is meningitis

 

Three conditions I would consider are hypoglycemia, stroke, and traumatic brain injury.

Hypoglycemia occurs when blood glucose falls too low, preventing the brain from receiving enough energy to function normally. It can cause confusion, unusual behavior, sweating, or unconsciousness. A stroke can interfere with blood flow to the brain, producing sudden confusion, difficulty speaking, weakness, or other neurological changes. A traumatic brain injury can result from a fall or impact to the head and may cause confusion, memory problems, or decreased consciousness. I would keep all three possibilities in mind until my assessment provides more information.


  

